<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44779" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπῐθ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπειθής</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ πείσεις νιν, οὐ γὰρ εὐπιθής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					335
				</span></i>
			: here and in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				274
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				259
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				829
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				623
			</span></i> cod. 
				Med.
			 has -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειθ</span>-, but -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῐθ</span>- is required by the metre in
				<u>Pr.</u>l. c. and is possible elsewh. (but in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				982
			</span></i> (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πιθ</span>- codd.) the metre perh.
			favours -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειθ</span>-); the sense is sts. 
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνείρων φάσματ᾽
				εὐπ̔ἐιθῆ σέβεις</span>; <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				274
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σήματ᾽ εὐπ̔ἐιθῆ
					βροτοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ch.</u>
					259
				</span></i>
			; perh. also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος
					εὐπ̔ἐ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιθές</span></span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				982
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημηγόρους . .
					εὐπ̔ἐιθεῖς στροφάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Supp.</u>
					623
				</span></i>
			 (s. v.l.); sts. 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δ᾽ εὐπ̔ἐιθὴς ἐμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Eu.</u>
					829
				</span></i>
			, cf. <u>Pr.</u> l.c.</div>
